ai-self-study license scope

Original educational text in book/chapters, book/references.tex, README.md,
docs/, research/, original experimental figures in book/generated/, and the
original portions of the compiled PDF: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International (CC BY 4.0), see licenses/CC-BY-4.0.txt.
Attribution: ai-self-study contributors, repository ai-self-study.

Original Python, Shell, and test code in experiments/, scripts/, and tests/:
MIT License, see licenses/MIT.txt.

Generated numerical data in results/ and original QA findings may be reused
under CC BY 4.0. Attribution and a record of modifications help preserve
scientific provenance.

The fixed typesetting adapter embedded in book/main.tex was supplied through
the user's explicitly requested math-latex-typesetting skill and is distributed
in this deliverable under the user's source-delivery authorization. It is not
the official ElegantBook class. Its original provider's rights are retained;
this project does not independently assert that this inherited template is
covered by the project's MIT or CC BY grant. See docs/third-party.md.

External papers, course material, fonts, software dependencies, model weights
and datasets retain their own licenses. This repository contains no third-party
paper/book full text, downloaded model, copied course assignment, or bundled
font. Linking to a source does not relicense it.
